course: dictionary
lesson: 13562
title: Inaccurate: not exact, with mistakes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inaccurate means not correct or not exact. It contains mistakes. The prefix in- means not, and accurate means correct and exact, so inaccurate is the opposite of accurate. «My ruler gave an inaccurate length, because I started measuring from the chipped end.» The ruler is not broken; this measurement was not exact.
explain: In maths and science, a measurement or answer is inaccurate when it is not close to the true value. «Tom's answer was inaccurate, because he made a mistake when he added the numbers.» You can check a measurement by measuring again carefully, starting from the zero mark.
explain: Inaccurate also describes information. «The website said the Moon is made of cheese, which is inaccurate.» A fake fact is inaccurate, so before you believe something, check it against a trusted source.
fact: Inaccurate means not correct or not exact, and it contains mistakes.
fact: Accurate means correct and exact. Inaccurate is its opposite.
fact: The prefix in- means not, so inaccurate means not accurate.
fact: «An inaccurate ruler» gives measurements that are not exact.
fact: To avoid believing inaccurate facts, check information in more than one trusted source.
exercise: «The scale gave an inaccurate weight, so we weighed the apple again.» What does inaccurate mean? | Very heavy | Shiny | *Not correct or not exact | Brand new
exercise: «Mia's answer was inaccurate because she added the numbers wrongly.» Which word means the opposite of inaccurate? | Loud | *Accurate | Late
exercise: Which sentence has inaccurate information? | *Penguins can fly over the sea. | The Sun is a star. | Ice is cold.
test: «The measuring cup was inaccurate, so the cake had too much sugar.» What does inaccurate mean here? | *Not exact, with mistakes | Very large | Clean and shiny | Quick
test: A pupil wants to check an inaccurate measurement. What is the best thing to do? | Throw the ruler away | Guess a new number | *Measure again carefully | Never measure again
exam: «The report had inaccurate facts, so Sam checked two trusted websites before he believed it.» What does inaccurate mean in this sentence? | Printed in big letters | *Containing mistakes, not exact | Very long | Full of colourful pictures
